{
  "_comment": "Rules of the safety guard for claude-local sessions (scripts\\hooks\\Guard-Tool.ps1, docs\\security.md). The guard protects THIS machine and the user's own data from destructive tool calls of the local model. It does not judge what the model works on. 'deny' stops a call, 'ask' hands the decision to the user (in runs without a user, -p, an 'ask' counts as 'no'). Patterns are .NET regular expressions, matched case-insensitively against the whole command; in JSON every backslash is written twice. Paths may use %VARIABLES%; %CLAUDE_LOCAL_ROOT% is the install folder and %CLAUDE_LOCAL_PROJECTS% the projects folder of this machine (set by scripts\\_common.ps1), an entry with a variable this machine does not know is left out; %MyDocuments%, %MyPictures%, %MyMusic%, %MyVideos%, %DesktopDirectory% and %Startup% are the real folders of the user (Windows may have moved them). secretPaths, secretFileNames: asked before access (files in them are left out of searches). guardFiles, guardFolders: the protection itself; the folders do not count while someone works on the program itself. autostartPaths: files programs read or start by themselves, writing asks in every mode. protectedFiles: files of a project that run or are obeyed later by themselves, patterns on the path below the project with forward slashes; changing them asks in the modes ask and edits. After a change run scripts\\Test-Guard.ps1 and scripts\\Test-Security.ps1.",
